WEBVTT

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:07.490
What a nice morning.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.970
I guess it is a bit cold, though.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.150
Is this spot okay?

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.480
Yeah!

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.000
Looks good.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.160
We're all done, so why 
don't you go take a seat?

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.420
Yes, sir!

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:26.000
Sorry to be asking for 
your help on our day off.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.520
It's fine.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.310
It's not like I had anything 
to do this morning.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:33.700
But yeah, yesterday was a lot of fun, huh?

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.470
Yeah, I'm also happy that 
everybody liked my mom's mugs.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.240
This picture's good, too.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:49.150
Have you been worried 
about that forever now?

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.770
Oh, well...

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.960
It'll be the spot for Toyokawa 
Himeno's masterpiece.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.750
I don't know.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.580
Maybe it is weighing on me.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.560
There, there.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.930
<b>Good Day for the Pottery Wheel</b>

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.520
It might be a little too early still.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.960
It's been a while. I guess 
I'll take a walk around here.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.600
Prett<b>y</b>!

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.060
You're doing grea<b>t</b>!

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.370
That's fa<b>b</b>!

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.540
The one to put in the shelf!

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.100
Brillian<b>t</b>!

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.400
Why am I playing shiritori?

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:15.500
This pressure!

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.380
Or is it?

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.970
That's Tokikawa Himena's world, over there.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:33.490
Huh?

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:38.480
<b><i>Café Tokishirou</i></b>

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.580
Café Tokishirou.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.110
That's a happy name!

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:45.490
Let's talk about it tomorrow.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:45.490
Thank you so much!

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:45.490
Touko-senpai, I need your advice.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:43.050
Touko-senpai, I need your advice.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.490
Hime-chan, can you come down?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.500
Coming!

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:49.830
What is it?

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:53.700
I need you to take out an iced coffee 
for me and get an autograph.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.990
An autograph?

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.500
Arai Keitarou-san is here!

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.250
Who was that again?

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:00.500
Right here!

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.510
Don't you know him?

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.900
He was a big star in the Showa era.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:08.760
Wow! So what's such a famous 
person doing in Tajimi?

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:10.170
I'm not sure.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:14.270
He was in the area ages ago 
for a movie shoot, though.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.110
Here you go.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.060
A card for the autograph and an iced coffee.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.780
What, me?!

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.830
Thank you for waiting.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.030
Thanks.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.430
So, um...

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.690
Can you tell me where Juubeh kiln is?

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:32.370
I'm not quite sure which 
bus I need to get on.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.040
Uh, ah, the Juubeh kiln?

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.010
Oh, wait! I know!

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.960
My senpai's grandfather owns it.

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:41.010
Is that right?

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:45.820
It's been a while since I've been to Tajimi 
and all this walking around has got me worn out.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.710
We'll bring the car around.

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:50.060
It's quite a ways from here, right?

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.680
You can do that, right, Toki-kun?

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.170
Sure!

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:55.980
Oh, I couldn't.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.520
Oh, it's not a problem!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.740
You did a movie shoot in Tajimi 
a long time ago, right?

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.480
I was in high school when I went to see you.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.150
Did you now?

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.460
Well, what do you know?

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:12.020
No Bicycles
or Scooters

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:19.120
You know, my first leading role was playing 
a potter named Kawada Tokishirou.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.350
Tokishirou?

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:22.010
That's my dad's name, too.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.330
Oh, so that's why you came into our café.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.090
That's right. The sign made me so happy.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:32.040
You won the best leading actor 
award with that first role, right?

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.560
That's amazing!

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.750
Oh no. All of that happened so long ago.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.070
So are you a potter, too?

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:42.140
I just started.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:47.090
You're going to make something really wonderful and put it up in the café, right?

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.680
What?! You told him about that, too?

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:54.150
It's not funny!

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:59.130
So are you friends with 
my senpai's grandfather?

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:04.230
Back when I was cast for the movie, I didn't 
know the first thing about pottery.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:13.910
At the time, Aoki-sensei was an 
energetic potter in his thirties.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:17.840
He taught me the basics, but 
he was really kind to me.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.030
Wow, really?

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:21.630
I always thought of him 
as someone really strict.

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:23.120
Not at all.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.530
We kept in touch afterwards as well.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:30.520
When I'd sent him photos of my passionate 
but horrible attempt at a bowl,

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.340
he'd give me advice.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.850
He also made sure to watch movies where I had 
the leading role and sent me a written review.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.930
So he'll look at things Arai-san made...

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:44.700
He's never shown up, though.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.930
<i>I didn't see this coming...</i>

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.580
Wow, this is so different?!

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.400
What's going on, Touko-senpai?

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:56.400
Is it weird?

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.940
It's not weird at all! It's wonderful!

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.370
But I thought blue was your color!

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:05.860
The thing is, I've been wanting to try 
something like this for a long time.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.080
Oh, I see.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.880
So I just stopped worrying and did it.

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.370
Actually, I had somehow 
known she wanted this...

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:22.040
But I always liked the blue she created...

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:27.030
So I couldn't encourage her.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:31.750
You don't have to worry 
that it's not like you!

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:33.670
Toyokawa-san...

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.210
I'm a bit jealous.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.180
Why can Hime-chan just come 
out and say it like that?

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:52.790
Mii-chan, good cat.

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:53.620
Huh?

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:00.320
Hello! It's been so long, Arai-san!

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.900
Touko-chan?

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:04.990
Wow, you've really grown!

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:06.550
You look wonderful.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.140
Thank you!

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:11.240
Is Aoki-sensei in the usual spot?

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.350
Yes, please go in.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.650
Toyokawa-san?

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:23.830
Oh, you came with him.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:27.320
These are some sandwiches and 
coffee from my grandmother.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.000
She's a big fan of Arai-san.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.140
I see!

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:31.770
So, uh...

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:33.720
Later, we could have that talk?

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:35.180
Huh?

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:37.270
Touko-chan!

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.410
Where's the bathroom again?

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.460
Just in the back there.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:43.750
Come with me.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.030
Thank you.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:49.370
I'm so sorry to come unannounced.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.850
Oh, no. Please don't be so formal.

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:55.690
But anyway, it's really been a while, huh?

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:59.320
I apologize for being such 
an incompetent student.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.150
I'm glad to see you in good health.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:05.430
So how has it been with your grandfather?

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.190
Nothing's really changed.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:11.020
I still haven't had a chance 
to show him the big plate.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.620
I see.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.240
Touko-chan.

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:18.030
Will you join me? It's been so long.

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:23.030
This is quite hard.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:27.510
Oh, no! Not like that.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:29.620
You got careless.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:32.970
I'm embarrassing.

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:38.890
Just what I'd expect from you, Touko-chan.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.350
That's perfect.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.560
Not at all...

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:45.440
Your movements are stiff, Touko.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.270
Sorry.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.880
Are they?

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.870
I can tell by looking at the 
muscles in her right arm.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:54.630
You're putting too much force into it.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:58.010
He's too hard on you, huh, Touko-chan?

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:00.860
No, I really was getting too stiff.

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:10.550
Talking about being hard.

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:14.360
My father was also hard on me,
 in a different way.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:18.350
He's never praised my work, not even once.

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.950
But you're such a great actor.

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:21.840
Right?

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:26.820
He was the type of person who wouldn't accept 
anything but governmental work or banking.

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:31.230
When he found out I was becoming an actor, 
he said he'd disown me and cut me off.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:35.030
There were many people like that, back then.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:38.860
I figured I'd just cut 
him out of my life, too.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.190
But at some point I realized,

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:44.630
I was trying to put on performances 
that would make my old man praise me.

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.420
Is that how things go?

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:54.910
However at the wake, my sister 
showed me a notebook.

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:59.040
There were 30 years worth of clippings 
about me from magazines and papers...

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.790
And he had written,
 "This performance made me cry hard."

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:07.120
"He might not be the best, 
but he's become a first-rate actor."

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:09.400
That's quite something.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:13.420
The moment I saw that, 
my heart felt so much lighter.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:17.080
It was right after that that 
I won an award in France.

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:20.860
It's so great that there 
was such a notebook.

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:26.220
I would have liked to reconcile 
with him before he died, though.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:32.760
We don't have to talk today, Touko-senpai.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:34.210
Huh, are you sure?

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:38.380
Yeah, I kind of...

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.560
Thank you so much for everything today.

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:46.700
Of course. Please take care.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:57.770
Then I guess I'll go too, Grandpa.

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:58.730
Touko,

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:02.120
do you have some time?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.330
You really helped me out today.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.130
No, thank you! I had such a fun day!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:17.630
<b>To Tokikawa Sachie-san 
Arai Keitarou</b>

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:16.510
This is for your grandmother.

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:20.040
Wow, thank you so much!

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:24.770
I'm sorry. All we did was 
talk about ancient history.

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:27.250
Not at all! It was very inspiring!

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:28.740
I'm glad to hear that.

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:32.980
So now I have yet another reason 
to come back to Tajimi.

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:37.650
I'll see you again at your café for 
some sandwiches and fresh coffee.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:38.940
Definitely!

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:52.500
It's been so long since 
we've come here together.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.390
Yes.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:01.110
The fall leaves are so beautiful...

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:03.560
Yes.

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:28.460
The bob-haired one gets a sudden 
invitation from Forehead.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:35.310
<b>Mini-Mini Pottery Club</b>

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:32.620
The truth that gets revealed there is 
quite unexpected for the bob-haired one.

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:35.520
Our next episode is "Beyond 
the Calm Autumn Sky."

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>Next time:</b>

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>Beyond the Calm Autumn Sky</b>

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:39.600
No matter when or where, when the going 
gets rough, someone's got your back.
